{"author":{"id":"f4f7e123ea38957901744390924e1710825e6d55b5113472173231f66fb2d926"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781394905,"nonce":"DnNXJ9F42ToqrNbqsl7MSCFEOqM=","title":"Compiler: codegen can emit unbounded C (runaway loop filled disk with 384 GB paren.c)","message":"Incident (2026-06-13): a `gwbasic-compile paren.bas -o paren.c` run entered a\nnon-terminating code-generation loop and wrote a 348+ GB paren.c into its /tmp\nworking dir, growing ~30 MB/s. It was caught at ~384 GiB with the root\nfilesystem on track to fill in ~10h (a machine-wide outage). The process was in\nstate D at 100% CPU; killing it and removing the file reclaimed the space.\n\nRoot cause (class): a codegen path that emits via EMIT() but fails to advance\nthe token pointer `tp`, so an enclosing driver/expression loop re-emits the same\nfragment forever. The partial output was full of `gw_fn_instr(` calls,\nimplicating the INSTR / string-expression emission path.\n\nContext: the runaway ran at ~13:46 EDT on the WIP \"shared string-expr dispatch\"\ncode on branch feat/extern-followups (checked out 13:18, committed 19:20 as\n818562b, merged to main as 7627185). That intermediate state has been\nsuperseded; committed HEAD does not reproduce the runaway under a sweep of\nINSTR/paren inputs, so the specific non-advancing path is not yet pinned.\n\nMitigation shipped: output-size guard in the C backend.\n- EMIT() now counts bytes written to the real output file (scratch memstreams\n  excluded) and aborts cleanly once a cap is exceeded, removing the partial\n  file. codegen.c (codegen_overflow); codegen.h (codegen_opts_t.max_output_bytes,\n  out_path); compiler_main.c (--max-output-size MB, default 256, 0 = unlimited).\n- Verified: 74/74 tests/programs compile (largest legit output ~10 KB, ~25000x\n  under the default); guard fires at exit 2 with a clear diagnostic and removes\n  the partial file; 63/63 compiler tests pass.\n\nRemaining work:\n- Pin the specific non-advancing emit path (likely INSTR start-arg detection via\n  peek_is_string_expr, or a paren-mismatch branch) and fix it at the source.\n- Add a token-progress assertion in the statement / expression driver loops\n  (abort if `tp` did not advance across an iteration) as defense-in-depth.\n- Add a regression test once the trigger input is reconstructed.","files":null}]}